       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **The order as written:** 2550 mg three times daily comes to 7,650 mg/day.\n- **The maximum:** The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day, and the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin per dose is 1,000 mg. This order is three times the daily maximum, which risks severe lactic acidosis.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum total daily dose.\n- **2,550 mg/day total.** This could be split differently, for example 1,000 mg in the morning, 500 mg at midday, and 1,000 mg in the evening. Metformin is usually started low (500 mg once or twice daily) and titrated up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether the patient is starting metformin or already taking it. I'll enter the order once you confirm."
